<Group width=100% height=100%>
    <ImportSettings><SiteTheme /></ImportSettings>
    <Stacker id=authoring_content x=50% y=80px width={self.compact ? (100% - 48px) : 88%} autosize=true gutter=48px>
        <Stacker width={self.compact ? 100% : 82%} autosize=true gutter=24px>
            ///#h2
            <Text class="editorial_title" width=100%>Fluent in UI</Text>
            <Text class="editorial_lead" width=100%>Pax is a declarative UI language that combines HTML-like markup with spreadsheet-like expressions.</Text>
            <Text class="editorial_body" width=100%>Pax is designed to make user interface creation powerful, expressive, and fun.</Text>
        </Stacker>
        ///#ignore
        <SharedDefinitionDemo width=100% height={self.compact ? 610px : 330px} compact={self.compact}/>
        <Stacker width=100% autosize=true autosize_x=false autosize_y=true gutter={self.compact ? 32px : 6%}
            direction={self.compact ? StackerDirection::Vertical : StackerDirection::Horizontal}
            sizes={self.compact ? [] : [Some(60%), None]}>
            <Stacker width=100% autosize=true gutter=24px>
                ///#h3
                <Text class="editorial_subtitle" width=100%>Not a programming language, but a companion to one</Text>
                <Text class="editorial_body" width=100% markdown=true>Declarative `.pax` files sit alongside Rust. Describe your interface's structure, appearance, and relationships in Pax; write application logic with the full power of Rust. Changes to reactive Rust state flow through [Pax expressions](https://docs.pax.dev/data-binding-expressions.html), like updates through a spreadsheet.</Text>
                <Text class="editorial_lead" width=100%>Whether you're building a business application, a mobile app, an interactive art project, data visualizations, or a game—if it can be expressed in pixels, it can be built in Pax.</Text>
                <Text class="editorial_body" width=100% markdown=true>Want to see how it works? Open any **View Source** tab to see how that section was built, or explore the [website's source on GitHub](https://github.com/paxdotdev/pax/tree/main/pax-website).</Text>
            </Stacker>
            ///#ignore
            <CalculatorPreview width=100% height={(self.calculator_height)px} content_height=bind:self.calculator_height
                compact=true live={!self.compact}/>
        </Stacker>
    </Stacker>
    <Rectangle class="site_rule" x=50% y={100% - 1px} width={self.compact ? (100% - 48px) : 88%} height=1px/>
    <Rectangle class="site_ink" width=100% height=100%/>
</Group>

@settings {
    @mount: handle_mount
    @pre_render: handle_pre_render
}
